  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Pointer cursor",
      "text": "By default, radio input and label have `cursor: default` (same as native `input[type=\"radio\"]`).\nTo change cursor to pointer, set `cursorType` on [theme](/theming/theme-object/):",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Radio with tooltip",
      "text": "You can change target element to which tooltip is attached with `refProp`:\n\n- If `refProp` is not set, the tooltip is attached to the checkbox input\n- If `refProp=\"rootRef\"` is set, the tooltip is attached to the root element (contains label, input and other elements)",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Radio.Indicator",
      "text": "`Radio.Indicator` looks exactly the same as `Radio` component, but it does not\nhave any semantic meaning, it's just a visual representation of radio state. You\ncan use it in any place where you need to display radio state without any interaction\nrelated to the indicator. For example, it is useful in cards based on buttons, trees, etc.\n\nNote that `Radio.Indicator` cannot be focused or selected with keyboard. It is not\naccessible and should not be used as a replacement for `Radio` component.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Radio.Card component",
      "text": "`Radio.Card` component can be used as a replacement for `Radio` to build custom\ncards/buttons/other things that work as radios. The root element of the component\nhas `role=\"radio\"` attribute, it is accessible by default and supports the same\nkeyboard interactions as `input[type=\"radio\"]`.\n\nYou can use `Radio.Card` with `Radio.Group` the same way as `Radio` component:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "text": "Set `aria-label` or `label` prop to make the radio accessible:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
